WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.510
OK.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.610
Now, this is sort of funny, but some people
are furious.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:04.610
Why?

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.540
Because people are furious about everything
these days.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.670
Bomb throwing.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.080
Right wing radio host Rush Limbaugh quoted
me yesterday.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.240
He actually read one of my tweets.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.250
And it was one of the tweets I sent during
the stream of the first night of the Democratic

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.530
National Convention.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.830
At the time, I didn't think it was going particularly
well because it wasn't.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.900
So I'm going to play the clip of Rush for
you.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.960
Then I will talk about the reaction from some
on the left to this and just how completely

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.230
misguided and and missing the boat.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.280
Some people are about this.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.859
Let's look at Rush's clip.

00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:41.680
First, David Pakman political TV radio show
host tweeted, Someone please talk me off the

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.680
ledge.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.629
I want to win the first 22 minutes of this
convention.

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:46.629
I'm scared.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:49.039
Can somebody tell me how great this is or
something?

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:53.710
Can somebody make me feel better?

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:54.710
Didn't start well.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:59.129
OK, so the exact tweet that he read, he added
a paraphrase at the end, which is Make me

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:00.129
feel better.

00:01:00.129 --> 00:01:01.129
I didn't actually tweet that.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:02.129
I tweeted.

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:06.600
22 minutes into night, one quote, someone
please talk me off the ledge.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.830
I want to win.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.300
And the first 22 minutes of this DNC, I'm
scared.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.110
Can someone tell me how great this is or something?

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:18.370
Now, later on, it improved than I said it
did, particularly with Michelle Obama's speech

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:19.370
at the end of the night.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:23.170
And 92 was significantly better than night
one overall.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.350
But here's what I want to talk about with
you.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.610
I mentioned earlier and yesterday.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.750
That some people on the left were mad at me.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.710
They were even furious at me.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:40.030
I even had a few cancelations for lack of
a better term, because I was criticizing the

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:46.750
first part of night, one of the DNC, and there
were people on the left reacting with, you

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:51.150
know, this feeling of how does David have
the audacity to criticize what the DNC is

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.260
doing?

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:58.159
That I'm the problem because I'm pointing
out that I don't like some of this stuff and

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:03.040
I'm being mean and I'm not being supportive
of enough of removing Donald Trump or being

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.460
a team player or whatever.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:13.599
That is exactly the B.S. garbage tone, policing,
gatekeeping nonsense that leads us to losing.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:19.200
And some people said, David, when you tweeted
that you literally created fodder for the

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.239
right in the sense that Rush Limbaugh then
read your tweet.

00:02:23.239 --> 00:02:26.540
But the DNC was not going well at that point
in time.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.230
I didn't like what I saw.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.790
The right was going to say it was terrible
no matter what.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:36.599
So it wouldn't make a difference in that sense
because the right is going to come out and

00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:40.379
say, this is terrible and what an embarrassment
and blah, blah, blah.

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:42.659
I said what I believed to be going on.

00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:43.659
And you know what?

00:02:43.659 --> 00:02:44.659
Later on it improved than I said.

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:52.599
So I'm not saying it improved because of what
I said, but who gains anything from me lying

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:55.930
to you and saying, wow, this is really great.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.749
This is this is going so well.

00:02:57.749 --> 00:03:03.980
And so when I see these comments, oh, you
ended up supporting Republican talking points

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.370
by tweeting that.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.900
No, I reacted genuinely.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.150
That's the promise.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.150
That's the premise and the promise of this
program.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.629
My commitment here is not always to say what
you think.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:21.709
It's not to be onboard with whatever is the
orthodoxy of the Democratic Party.

00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:23.459
I'm not even a Democrat.

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:28.819
Remember, the reason people watch the live
streams and the content is to get my honest

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:31.419
and immediate reactions to what's going on.

00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:36.700
What do we gain if I do political theater
where I say, you know, this is crap, but it

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.519
would look bad if I say that.

00:03:38.519 --> 00:03:42.720
So I'm going to pretend that this is great
and lie to my audience.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.269
Like, is that actually what people are suggesting
I should do?

00:03:46.269 --> 00:03:49.189
Because Rush Limbaugh read one of my tweets.

00:03:49.189 --> 00:03:55.760
The fact that Limbaugh read a tweet is no
more evidence of anything than the fact that

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:00.349
Hitler breathing oxygen says anything about
oxygen.

00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:05.109
More broadly, if you understand the point
that I'm making, alluding to an ad hominem

00:04:05.109 --> 00:04:06.180
fallacy here.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:14.219
And so we really gain nothing by scolding
people who are making what are honest critiques.

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:21.470
And we actually I would make the case lose
a lot when we do this tone policing and attempting

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.290
to regulate what counts as acceptable commentary.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.770
And I was out of line, apparently, with what
is really a pretty milquetoast tweet, guys.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.340
I mean, in the end, this tweet is nothing's
hinging on this tweet.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.950
So I think it's interesting.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:40.150
I don't know exactly how my tweet made it
to Rush Limbaugh.

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:46.740
Now, years ago, Rush Limbaugh did a whole
segment where he refers to this program and

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.560
a segment we did multiple times without calling
it by name.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.110
And so we know that somehow, over time, clips
have gotten to Rush Limbaugh.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:58.110
I don't know how this got to him, quite frankly,
but somehow it did.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:05.890
But listen, if if you want a show that will
just always praise what the Democratic Party

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.940
is doing, I'm sure those shows exist.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.190
It's just not this one.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.190
OK.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:15.850
And so I'm not apologizing and I will continue
to call it like it is August.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:20.370
Twenty third is the 15th anniversary of the
David Pakman show.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:24.760
We will be doing a huge membership special
if you want to be notified about it.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.730
Just get on my newsletter at David Pakman
dot com.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.350
August twenty third e-mail.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:34.040
We'll go out telling you how to take advantage
of what we hope will be the biggest single

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.970
day surge in memberships in David Pakman show
history.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:42.330
And of course, remember that you can get the
podcast on any app you like Spotify, Stitcher,

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:46.160
Google, Play, I, iTunes, Pandora.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:50.280
If that is your gig, get the daily audio podcast.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.470
Take it with you every single day.

